From eee034043946af803fe9c0dc213086c3967b45fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:22:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(gitops): turn the GitOps page into a three-step
 setup (BYT-10423)

The page opens with the outcome in one sentence, a line that says setup
writes files for GitHub Actions and GitLab CI, and three steps:
Databases, Workload identity and Workflow files. The step row sits on
top and Back and Continue sit in a sticky footer. Nothing is saved.

- Databases: a database group (recommended) or databases with an
  environment, and the deploy order by environment.
- Workload identity: pick or create one. The Create dialog offers
  GitHub Actions and GitLab CI only, closes after Create and picks the
  new identity. An identity for another OIDC provider cannot be picked,
  and one with no role blocks Continue with a link to Members. The git
  provider's logo shows before its name.
- Workflow files: the migration folder (editable), the repository when
  the identity names one, and every file for the identity's git
  provider. A file longer than 12 lines shows its first 12 lines until
  "Show all N lines". Copy always takes the whole file.

A lone group, database or identity is picked when the page opens. An
unset External URL does not block the steps: the alert shows on every
step, the files show {EXTERNAL_URL} marked, and copy is off.

Removed: the overview, the checklist, the GitHub/GitLab tabs, the
self-hosted runner switch, the test section, the old generators, the
workflow image and the strings only they used.
